# Empower Jace with a Jace planeswalker token already under your control: "If you control a Jace planeswalker token, you can't
# choose to create a new one" - the counters go on it (CR 701.71a). Bot1 casts Theorist's Proxy twice in one turn: the first
# makes the Jace token with 3 loyalty, the second puts three more on that same token (6), and only one Jace token exists.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Theorist's Proxy
Theorist's Proxy
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Theorist's Proxy.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 3
Bot1.Hand.Theorist's Proxy.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Jace Token; Mox Sapphire; Theorist's Proxy; Theorist's Proxy
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 6
